course: dictionary
lesson: 12792
title: Elaborate: many details
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Elaborate» is a word with two jobs. As an adjective, it describes something with many parts or details, like a costume with lace, ribbons and tiny beads. As a verb, to elaborate means to give more details or explain more.
explain: «The cake had an elaborate pattern of roses, swirls and stars.» The clue is the long list of small details. Elaborate does not just mean big. It means carefully made, with lots of parts that fit together.
explain: When a teacher says, «Can you elaborate on your answer?», she wants more than a short reply. Add details and examples. «The plant grew.» becomes «The plant grew three centimetres in a week because it sat in the sunshine.»
fact: Elaborate is pronounced ih-LAB-er-it as an adjective, and ih-LAB-er-ate as a verb.
fact: «Elaborate» as an adjective means having many parts or details, and carefully planned.
fact: «Elaborate» as a verb means to give more details or explain more.
fact: «An elaborate plan» is a plan with many steps and careful details.
fact: A useful phrase is «elaborate on», as in «Please elaborate on your idea.»
exercise: «The bride wore an elaborate dress covered in lace and tiny pearls.» What does elaborate mean here? | Very short | Plain and simple | *Having many detailed parts | Torn and dirty
exercise: «Can you elaborate on your answer?» What is the teacher asking you to do? | Say your answer more quietly | Write it in capital letters | Stop talking | *Add more detail and examples
exercise: «The magician performed an elaborate trick with three silver rings.» Find and copy one word that means carefully made with many details. | performed | *elaborate | magician | silver
test: What does elaborate mean in «elaborate decorations»? | Small and quick to make | Simple and plain | *Detailed, with many parts | Broken
test: Ravi wrote a one-line answer. His teacher said, «Please elaborate.» What should Ravi do? | *Give more details and examples | Write less | Ask his friend to write it | Rub out his answer
exam: «Mia wanted to elaborate on her plan, so she described each step in detail.» What does elaborate on mean here? | Hide it | Shorten it | Forget it | *Explain more fully, with extra detail
